  "id": "dysarthria",
  "term": "dysarthria",
  "definition": "Dysarthria is a motor speech problem in which speech sounds are not articulated clearly because the muscles of the face, tongue, larynx, or pharynx are not working together properly. It can occur with disorders affecting the nerves or brain systems that control these muscles, while language abilities themselves remain intact.",
